Thank you for asking me directly, and not guessing (or assuming) any =
candidate's position.=20

I will admit, I find it concerning that of all the questions that could =
be asked of a candidate for Connecticut State Senate, the one question =
you have chosen is whether I will publicly disavow the President of the =
United States. No sir, I will not, past, present or future.=20

I do not believe Americans should be required to answer for or denounce =
the President during the previous administration, and I do not believe =
that should be the standard now. I may not agree with outcomes, but I =
respect our constitution, and our process. That does not mean I agree =
with everything the person says, does, or communicates. I don't. But I =
don't take responsibility for someone else's words or actions. I take =
responsibility for mine.

I think one of the greatest challenges facing our society is that we =
increasingly define people by which political figures they support, =
oppose, are willing to denounce, or letter next to their name... rather =
than asking them what they actually believe. That leaves very little =
room for independent thought, disagreement, conversation or common =
ground.=20

I am running for the Connecticut State Senate. The people of the 4th =
District deserve leadership focused on Connecticut, affordability, =
taxes, education, housing, public safety, workforce and the policies =
coming out of Hartford. Those are the issues on which I am asking voters =
to judge me and, if elected, hold me accountable. I have lot=E2=80=99s =
to say and offer on all of that. So I welcome another question: one that =
relates to Connecticut, the 4th Senate District, or an issue I would =
actually have the responsibility and authority to address as your state =
senator.

Wishing you a wonderful Sunday! :)=20

Jenn Jennings
C: (203) 561-6105
jennjennings4senate@gmail.com


=EF=BF=BC=20

> On Sep 10, 2026, at 12:26=E2=80=AFAM, Scott Sauyet =
<scott.sauyet@gmail.com> wrote:
>=20
> Dear Ms. Jennings,
>=20
> I live in Andover, in the 4th Senate District, so you are on my ballot =
in November. I write about local government at andoverct.info =
<http://andoverct.info/>, and I should say plainly that I co-chair the =
Andover Democratic Town Committee. This letter is my own, sent in my own =
name.
>=20
> I have one question, and I would rather put it to you directly than =
guess at the answer.
>=20
> Will you publicly disavow Donald Trump?
>=20
> By that I mean a statement in your own name that he does not represent =
you and does not have your support. Not a comment on a single policy, =
and not a statement about the party in general.
>=20
> I am asking the same question, in the same words, of Ryan Fazio, Steve =
Weir, and Jason Guidone. Whatever you send me I will publish in full and =
unedited, with the question and the date, at =
http://andoverct.info/reports/ahm/disavowal/. If you would rather answer =
somewhere else, in the Rivereast or on your own page, that is fine. =
Point me to it and I will link it.
>=20
> If you have already answered this publicly and I have missed it, send =
me the link and I will say so.
>=20
> I plan to publish on September 17, 2026 and to update through the =
election. There is no deadline. An answer at any point gets added.
>=20
> Thank you for your time.
>=20
> Scott Sauyet
> Andover
> scott.sauyet@gmail.com <mailto:scott.sauyet@gmail.com>

